post_install() {
  cat <<'EOF'
This package installs `t3code` (desktop app) and `t3` (server).

The server keeps its old shape: same `t3 serve` command line, same base
directory (~/.t3), same port (3773), so existing pairings keep working.

`~/.local/bin/t3` comes before /usr/bin on PATH. Where such a launcher from an
older standalone install exists, it keeps running that runtime, so point it at
this package instead:

  ln -sfn /usr/bin/t3 ~/.local/bin/t3

Then restart whatever runs the server, from the same directory as before.
`t3 update` and `t3 uninstall` refuse on a package-managed install; use the
package manager instead.
EOF
}

post_upgrade() {
  cat <<'EOF'
Restart the running server so it picks up the new binary.
EOF
}
